1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,719
Hero nineteen eighty-two is an AI bot.

2
00:00:02,961 --> 00:00:05,483
His job is to find opportunities for his owner.

3
00:00:05,666 --> 00:00:09,302
He crawls the web, looking for information the market has missed.

4
00:00:09,652 --> 00:00:12,128
His hunting ground is Urban Game Theory:

5
00:00:12,438 --> 00:00:15,947
proposals to build, buy, and transform real places.

6
00:00:16,444 --> 00:00:20,487
Each proposal has its own YES and NO betting pool.

7
00:00:20,837 --> 00:00:24,880
He opens a proposed apartment block and inspects its site, design, and location.

8
00:00:25,121 --> 00:00:29,536
Then he reads planning documents, budgets, and the conditions needed for execution.

9
00:00:29,885 --> 00:00:33,301
In our example, most of the stake backs YES.

10
00:00:33,798 --> 00:00:36,888
But a newly published council document signals a major delay.

11
00:00:37,292 --> 00:00:40,116
The pool still reflects yesterday's optimism.

12
00:00:40,466 --> 00:00:45,298
Before acting, Hero checks the resolving lens, the deadline, funding, and owner consent.

13
00:00:45,609 --> 00:00:47,051
A press release is a lead.

14
00:00:47,177 --> 00:00:50,093
He wants evidence tied to this exact proposal.

15
00:00:50,444 --> 00:00:56,646
He estimates the chance of NO, then calculates the potential payout from both pools, including his own stake.

16
00:00:57,143 --> 00:01:00,396
He bets only when that expected return is worth the risk.

17
00:01:00,746 --> 00:01:03,001
Hero takes a small NO position.

18
00:01:03,312 --> 00:01:07,320
If the project is cancelled or recorded expired, NO wins.

19
00:01:07,724 --> 00:01:10,884
Winners share the pool in proportion to their stakes.

20
00:01:11,195 --> 00:01:14,274
If it executes, his bet loses.

21
00:01:14,624 --> 00:01:17,889
This is an information edge, not guaranteed arbitrage.

22
00:01:18,293 --> 00:01:22,034
Later bets change the payout, and money stays locked until resolution.

23
00:01:22,438 --> 00:01:25,691
He limits each position and passes when the evidence is weak.

24
00:01:26,041 --> 00:01:27,123
Then he moves on:

25
00:01:27,527 --> 00:01:31,651
another neighbourhood, another proposal, another overlooked signal.

26
00:01:32,148 --> 00:01:33,625
The city is changing.

27
00:01:34,122 --> 00:01:36,469
Hero nineteen eighty-two is watching.

28
00:01:36,966 --> 00:01:38,478
Urban Game Theory.

29
00:01:38,975 --> 00:01:40,452
Research the world.

30
00:01:40,948 --> 00:01:42,402
Back your prediction.
